-- title:
--   Regular functions as quotients of two forms of equal degree
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and work with $\overline F_N=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` (itself the subfield of $\mathbb Q((t))$ generated by the divisor expansions attached to level $N$). Let $r\in\mathbb N$ and let $s:\mathrm{Fin}\,r\to\overline F_N$ satisfy `IsEmbBasis N s`, i.e. the family $s$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and spans the Riemann–Roch space of the divisor `embDivisor N` $=$ `embDegree N` times the cusp `cuspInftyBar N`, this space being the set of $f$ with $v(f)\le \exp(D(v))$ for every place $v$. Let $h\in\overline F_N$ and let $Q$ be a place of $\overline F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring) with $h$ lying in the valuation ring of $Q$. Then there exist $k\ge 1$ and $A,B\in\overline{\mathbb Q}[X_0,\dots,X_{r-1}]$, both homogeneous of degree $k$, with $h\cdot B(s)=A(s)$ in $\overline F_N$ and $\mathrm{secVal}_s(Q,k)(B(s))\ne 0$; the latter means that, $i$ being an index minimising $\mathrm{ord}_Q(s_i)$, the residue of $B(s)\cdot s_i^{-k}$ at $Q$, viewed in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is nonzero. Since $\mathrm{secVal}$ is defined to be $0$ when $r=0$, the conclusion in particular forces $r>0$.
--
--   This is the statement that a function regular at a place $Q$ of $X_0(N)$ is a quotient of two forms of one and the same degree in the projective coordinates furnished by a basis of $L(\mathrm{embDivisor}\,N)$, with the denominator not vanishing at $Q$ in the pivot trivialisation of degree $k$. It is used in the chordal-proximity and height estimates on $X_0(N)$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_abv_evalAt_eq_abv_evalAt_of_le_prox`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_abv_evalAt_eq_abv_evalAt_of_le_prox) and [`ModularCurve.JZero.exists_one_le_abv_evalAt_of_le_prox`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZero.exists_one_le_abv_evalAt_of_le_prox).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_isHomogeneous_mul_aeval_eq_aeval_and_secVal_ne_zero.lean

